1
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
kick a pebble and even your shoes fly off.

3
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:32,920
Onto the head of the
carpenter I had in a chokehold,

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,300
lonely Kameari, one more yawn,
nothing has changed.

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,180
the streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed roof of the water tower,

9
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset falls into the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too, this is how it ends

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,740
Katsushika Shibamata, happiness again.

12
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:24,500
Having run around everywhere,
I finally realized I'm such a fool.

13
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:31,340
Fly! Patrol car cable car!

14
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:42,640
We blew through them! Perfect timing!

15
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:50,000
The suspect who robbed the Dasubikin Go Aotoshiden
of 800 million yen in cash is on the run.

16
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,600
The suspect's car is a black Fairlady X.

17
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:54,620
Nearby patrol cars, be on alert.

18
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:56,220
Roger.

19
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:58,180
Let's go, Maria-chan.

20
00:01:58,180 --> 00:01:59,720
Okay, Neiko-san.

21
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:02,440
Cosmo's name isn't bad, you know.

22
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:06,100
If we connect to the satellite we launched,

23
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:09,720
we can get exact ground
movements from Navicon.

24
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:13,840
Maria-chan,
can you pinpoint the suspect's car?

25
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:14,380
Yes.

26
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:18,740
The maker is...
an old man's car, the Fairlady X.

27
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:21,000
Five cars are running within two kilometers.

28
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,460
The color is black.

29
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:24,420
We've narrowed it down to one.

30
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:28,120
Reading the plate number via UTMS.

31
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:30,940
It's a stolen car, with three occupants.

32
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:32,500
No doubt about it.

33
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,460
What? A police car!

34
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:43,780
When did they get here?!

35
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:47,760
You in the Fairlady! Stop immediately!

36
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:50,820
What's with the disrespect?!

37
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:52,540
As if we'd let you catch us!

38
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:54,800
Alright, lose them!

39
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:57,720
Yeah! Let me show you the skills
of an eternal license holder!

40
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:01,040
You plan to run all the way

41
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:07,520
Damn it!

42
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:12,620
Time to teach them a lesson.

43
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:13,300
Yes.

44
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,120
A gift from Super Cosmo.

45
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:31,700
I'm placing you under arrest.

46
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:39,120
If you so much as try anything funny,

47
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:45,200
the latest patrol car,
trial-adopted by Katsushika Police Station,

48
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:47,920
Cosmo's success truly
has been a winning streak.

49
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:52,000
Not to mention the performance of Cosmo,
equipped with the latest systems,

50
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,000
the achievements of Officers Reiko Akimoto
and Ai Asato can't be overlooked either.

51
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:59,980
there are many men across Japan
who want to be arrested by these two.

52
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:01,480
Currently at Katsushika Police Station,

53
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:03,740
They've really become popular, those two.

54
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:07,560
We'd want a patrol car like that too

55
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:10,620
Senpai, you didn't know?

56
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:16,080
In fact, the new patrol car jointly
developed with America is arriving here today.

57
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:17,480
What, seriously?

58
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,320
It's true.

59
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:30,320
Well, this is amazing.

60
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:36,120
Looks like you like it, Mr. Gorilla.

61
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:38,080
So you're the one?

62
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:42,660
Professor Ezaki!
Then who developed this new patrol car?

63
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:47,800
That's right! It's the famous
super patrol car I developed, anyway.

64
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:51,800
It's the Ezaki G1!

65
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:57,080
Wow, what a truly wonderful car.

66
00:04:57,580 --> 00:04:59,080
Were you with the Chief too?

67
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:03,840
Ryotsu, rejoice! You've been chosen
as the driver of this super patrol car!

68
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:04,920
Me, really?

69
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:08,500
Really? But didn't that guy develop it?

70
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:09,982
Exactly.

71
00:05:10,032 --> 00:05:15,400
The Ezaki Z1 is the greatest robot patrol car in history,
which I developed.

72
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:18,900
A robot patrol car?
Does it transform or something?

73
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:22,115
No, no.
It's equipped with artificial intelligence,

74
00:05:22,165 --> 00:05:24,740
so it can make its own
decisions and act on them.

75
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:27,040
Hello. Nice to meet you.

76
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:29,105
Whoa, it talked.

77
00:05:29,155 --> 00:05:32,300
Is it really thinking
and speaking for itself?

78
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:35,180
Yes, I'm speaking of my own free will.

79
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:38,160
And the amazing part is that
it can do impressions too,

80
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:39,500
can it?

81
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:42,880
Ho ho, Giant, hello.

82
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:43,720
Ho ho ho.

83
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,940
That doesn't sound like him at all.

84
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:47,080
And a game for one-time use.

85
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:52,120
It's been running a bit more than usual.

86
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:57,900
I plan to pair it with me
and make it a comedy act.

87
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:01,740
You're already registered in the computer.

88
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:04,520
No matter what, you have to ride it,
or we're in trouble.

89
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:05,680
No way.

90
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:09,160
I thought it looked cool,
but of course it's your invention.

91
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,460
It's a worthless piece of junk.

92
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:11,440
You idiot!

93
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:15,820
What are you doing, Chief?

94
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:17,640
Watch your mouth.

95
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:20,400
I'm a sergeant, and I outrank you.

96
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:26,360
A car being a sergeant? That's ridiculous.

97
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:27,820
What are you talking about?

98
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:28,920
A salute battle, is it?

99
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:31,520
Yeah, yeah, this is fine, right?

100
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:35,540
That's wrong.
Please start over from the beginning.

101
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:40,500
I told you.

102
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:45,100
This Ezaki Z1 is a robot car
with artificial intelligence.

103
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:49,060
Get it? It's far more capable than you are.

104
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:53,900
But why would I be made the
driver of this Sergeant Z1,

105
00:06:54,824 --> 00:06:58,520
Well, it's an experimental assignment.

106
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,900
And there are all sorts of dangers involved.

107
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:05,720
Yes! With performance far
surpassing Maria and Reiko's Cosmo,

108
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:07,520
this Z1 needs a partner who

109
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:11,820
can get back up even after being run over by a tank.
Only you can do it, Gorilla.

110
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:14,060
Doesn't that mean it's a
matter of life and death?

111
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:17,120
Okay-ss!

112
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,060
This is the true frontier spirit!

113
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:20,480
The soul of Meerica!

114
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:23,260
You've gone all American-crazy
without even noticing!

115
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:25,920
After all, it's Professor Switch.

116
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:28,420
Over in Meerica, the water gushes beer!

117
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:33,280
King appeal!

118
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:36,120
A man who knows the difference,
Ezaki Kill-you-kyun!

119
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:38,260
Oh my, oh my, oh my, oh my,

120
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:40,940
Remember and write down
this graceful step...

121
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:43,140
Aren't you overdoing it, pretending
to read when you can't even read it?

122
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:44,800
Anyway, Ryotsu,

123
00:07:44,850 --> 00:07:47,700
From today, this Z1 is your direct superior!

124
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:51,000
Work hard every day,
washing and waxing the car!

125
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:51,700
Got it!

126
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:52,500
I'll be back!

127
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:53,200
Ken!

128
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:58,200
A car as my boss, honestly...

129
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:25,000
Ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow
ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow

130
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,040
That's right, as long as I keep my distance,
I've got the upper hand.

131
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:33,220
Boss, my foot! You're just a car, so don't
you dare talk back to me, you piece of junk!

132
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:34,480
You're naive, my friend.

133
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:45,020
If you run away again, I'll treat you
to something with even more firepower.

134
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:47,080
So the other one's better

135
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:51,880
Of course it is.
Its IQ is more than three times yours.

136
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:56,900
Well then, tell me the difference
between a male and a female crayfish.

137
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:02,580
The electrochemical patterns of
IC circuits are truly beautiful.

138
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:05,640
The Merick Gum computer industry
will conquer the world...

139
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:07,800
Your way of dodging is becoming Ezaki-like.

140
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:09,080
I can hear you.

141
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:13,260
Fine, you're my boss. I won't defy you.

142
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:15,840
Good. That's how it should be.

143
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:18,220
Sounds like a strict boss.

144
00:09:31,660 --> 00:09:33,680
Finally finished the waxing.

145
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:35,680
Sounds like it was quite a job.

146
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:39,360
After all,
it's a car built by that crazy professor.

147
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:43,680
I heard it was built to rival
Reiko's and Maria's Cosmo.

148
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:46,240
I wonder what special features it has.

149
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,000
Take a look at this.

150
00:09:53,240 --> 00:09:55,460
It's turned into a different car.

151
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:57,860
An unmarked patrol car, I see.

152
00:09:57,860 --> 00:10:00,940
With this,
nobody would think it's a patrol car!

153
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:08,320
Ryotsu-kun, put your hand on my door.

154
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,340
Like this?

155
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:14,680
Fingerprint match, it came up.

156
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:16,660
Ryotsu Kankichi, Junsaku Award.

157
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:19,380
Plastic model enthusiast,
a man who's sloppy with money.

158
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:23,420
Katsushika Award, survey: man who doesn't want to marry,
seven years running.

159
00:10:23,420 --> 00:10:24,300
Number one.

160
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:26,760
Don't put that kind of data in there!

161
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:31,580
Subordinates who defy me get punished!

162
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:41,240
That's a rather rough way of doing things.

163
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:44,400
Hi there, Ryo-chan, Kei-chan, Ryo-sama.

164
00:10:44,940 --> 00:10:46,460
Reiko and Maria.

165
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:50,100
We heard a rival had shown up,
so we came to take a look.

166
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:52,160
Some rival

167
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:55,240
Hello, Lady Reiko, Lady Maria.

168
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:57,820
The car just talked!

169
00:10:58,380 --> 00:11:00,580
I am Ezaki Z1.

170
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:03,600
I am a robot patrol car
with artificial intelligence.

171
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:05,800
Both of you are so beautiful.

172
00:11:06,340 --> 00:11:07,980
Aren't you clever.

173
00:11:07,980 --> 00:11:10,040
You're wrong, you know.

174
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:13,140
Reiko's a woman, but Maria's a man.

175
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:16,120
Hey, don't blow the tune.

176
00:11:16,460 --> 00:11:18,700
It's true! Hey, Maria!

177
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:19,640
Yeah.

178
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:22,540
Yeah, Maria's a man.

179
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:24,400
Maria's a man.

180
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:27,200
Reiko's a woman and Maria's a man.

181
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:29,000
Yeah, Maria's a man.

182
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,320
Come on, stop it! Don't overthink it!

183
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:33,360
Next thing you know, it'll break!

184
00:11:34,220 --> 00:11:35,520
Somehow...

185
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:54,960
But it really is the most eye-catching one.

186
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,680
Everyone's staring at us.

187
00:11:57,940 --> 00:12:00,480
Best of all, it drives itself, so it's easy.

188
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:05,420
What do you think you're doing,
putting your feet up on your superior?

189
00:12:09,220 --> 00:12:12,160
So they installed something
like this instead of airbags?

190
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:14,400
Keep your eyes on the road while driving.

191
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:15,740
Yeah, got it.

192
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:20,580
Then it's fine to listen to a CD, right?

193
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:33,620
This isn't my taste.

194
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:35,200
Switch to some Komuro-style music.

195
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,260
What are you doing?

196
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:37,980
I like listening to it, you know.

197
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:40,740
Are you saying you'll defy your superior?

198
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:43,580
Isn't that problematic in a lot of ways?

199
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:45,760
Getting knocked off the
fast track to promotion...

200
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:52,340
Alright, alright, I get it.
Quit with the snide remarks.

201
00:12:57,580 --> 00:13:01,760
Once again, a ridiculous comedy routine,
from the old days.

202
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:05,440
Didn't I tell you it's the Cosmo type?

203
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:10,380
Emergency call!

204
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:20,220
We know where the smugglers are meeting.
That warehouse up ahead.

205
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:24,120
Alright, our first chance right off the bat.
Don't lose, Twin Wen.

206
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:24,980
He's skipping the bill!

207
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:28,780
Two silver suspects,
caught in the act, spotted!

208
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:33,380
Not this way. Go back!

209
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:36,440
Oof, let go of me.

210
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:38,780
Not that way.

211
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:39,340
This way!

212
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:03,960
Firing gum-gum rounds!

213
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:05,020
Gum-gum rounds!

214
00:14:11,180 --> 00:14:11,940
What is this?

215
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:13,220
Stop your useless resistance.

216
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:14,240
You're under arrest.

217
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:18,860
Mitsuyu rounds are better than the dine-and-dash squad,
aren't they?

218
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:23,460
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

219
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:26,480
We're a little late from
the dine-and-dash squad, but

220
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:29,360
We've got gum-gum rounds and missiles,
and Mitsuyu rounds too!

221
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,720
We'll catch them all in one net!

222
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:32,920
The credit's ours!

223
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:34,060
Go!

224
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:40,040
Illegally parked vehicle spotted.

225
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:41,340
Moving immediately.

226
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:42,840
Not again.

227
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:44,840
Just leave it alone.

228
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:47,160
We can't let this crime slip by.

229
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:49,200
Firing heat rounds!

230
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:57,800
Hopeless.

231
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:04,760
Look at this.

232
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:08,580
There's not a single article about the Z1.

233
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:11,760
It's all about Maria and Reiko.

234
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:13,920
That's strange.

235
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:17,020
What is Japanese journalism even looking at?

236
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:19,820
You're going about it the wrong way.

237
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:23,140
At this rate,
Cosmo will leave us in the dust.

238
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:25,980
What do you think will happen then?

239
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:27,060
What will happen?

240
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:29,100
Of course it is.

241
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:32,980
The Z1 will be judged
incompetent and scrapped.

242
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:34,520
As scrap metal.

243
00:15:35,660 --> 00:15:38,380
No! No! No! No! No! No!

244
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:43,220
Then you'll do exactly as I say!

245
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:46,900
What? W-what should I do?

246
00:15:48,100 --> 00:15:50,780
The pattern the Japanese like best is,

247
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:52,940
the body and the anus!

248
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:54,920
It's Goto! Wait!

249
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:57,620
No, Goto, it's Goto!

250
00:15:57,620 --> 00:15:59,020
Aaaaaah!

251
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:04,160
Young one, wait!

252
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:07,100
Do you not see this inro?

253
00:16:07,620 --> 00:16:09,400
Since you ask,

254
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:14,400
What's this supposed to be?

255
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:17,520
Now! Fire the net rounds!

256
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:21,780
Damn it!

257
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:25,400
See? Just looking at the inro,
people instinctively bow their heads.

258
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:29,100
This brilliant strategy exploits
the Japanese people's habit,

259
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:33,200
How about that?

260
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,880
Do something flashy and you'll
get proper press coverage.

261
00:16:37,020 --> 00:16:37,740
I see.

262
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:41,460
As long as you keep doing what I say from now on,
you can't go wrong.

263
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:47,180
Listen, this is Japan, you know.

264
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:50,920
After all, we have to work at
appealing to the Japanese people.

265
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:52,480
Good.

266
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:55,602
I'll give you a special mission.

267
00:16:55,652 --> 00:16:59,000
Coach me on how to win
over the Japanese people.

268
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:00,140
Neheh.

269
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,040
Alright, leave it to me!

270
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:05,856
Listen, for songs,
go with enka or Naniwa-bushi.

271
00:17:05,906 --> 00:17:08,694
Treat your subordinates to meals generously,

272
00:17:08,744 --> 00:17:12,360
and above all, show some guts.
That's how you win them over!

273
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:13,480
Daaah!

274
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:22,980
Here you go! Generic ice water!
Your wait is over!

275
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:27,860
Sergeant, you can handle more, can't you!

276
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:31,000
The Two's Right to Win

277
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:36,160
The Last Patrol

278
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:37,520
Olé!

279
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:40,880
Hahahahahahaha

280
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:42,900
Ryo-san, you!

281
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:46,040
It's a blessing to have such good momentum,
isn't it?

282
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:47,560
Hey, Sergeant.

283
00:17:48,140 --> 00:17:51,720
And now, special drink service time!

284
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:54,960
I'll close the deal on
premium wax at 50% off.

285
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:57,800
The more you polish, the more shine you get.

286
00:17:57,800 --> 00:17:58,900
R-really?

287
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:02,000
Maybe I'll add another bottle.

288
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:05,520
Waiter, a new bottle, please.

289
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:09,620
Also, two bottles of WD-40, please.

290
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:13,480
Whoa, Sergeant-sama, I can't drink any more.

291
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,160
You idiot! One more round, let's go!

292
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:21,040
Ryotsu!

293
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:24,180
What are these receipts?

294
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,740
A yakitori bar,
a karaoke box, and a cabaret.

295
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:32,840
Come on, Chief.
It's all money the Sub-Inspector spent.

296
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:34,200
What did you say?

297
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:36,740
I was just treated to drinks.

298
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:40,800
Well, you'd be cursed if you turned
down your superior's invitation, right?

299
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:46,260
As expected of you, senior.
You've already tamed the Z1, it seems.

300
00:18:46,260 --> 00:18:48,840
The Z1 would never do something like that.

301
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:52,520
You made it do all of it, didn't you?
Confess!

302
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:59,480
Emergency alert: an international terrorist
wanted by Interpol has been spotted.

303
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:02,820
Why would those violent guys

304
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:05,720
Ryotsu,
go arrest them immediately in the Z1!

305
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:09,240
But peel off all those stickers on the way!

306
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:13,560
The terrorist is heading toward Tokyo Bay.

307
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:18,520
They're probably trying to
escape abroad by sea somehow.

308
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:20,280
What?

309
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,180
A car from behind!

310
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:26,440
There's a car approaching at top speed,
and it's -

311
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:28,740
It's Ryo-sama's car!

312
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:32,520
Go for it! Hey, you girls, let's race!

313
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:35,380
You're looking pretty sick.

314
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:37,840
It's because she's been
influenced by Ryo-chan.

315
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:41,940
Even the AI has changed its personality.
That's amazing.

316
00:19:41,940 --> 00:19:44,980
That's the best part about Ryo-sama,
his overflowing power.

317
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:48,260
But we can't lose the race
to arrest the criminal.

318
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:51,400
Rego-re has picked up speed! Don't lose!

319
00:19:58,520 --> 00:19:59,780
Don't get any closer!

320
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:02,060
Watch out!

321
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:12,280
Back off! Can't you see this window?

322
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:14,380
Do you really think that would surprise me?

323
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:21,980
Look out! I'm blasting you with missiles!
Fire everything!

324
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:22,440
So?

325
00:20:23,040 --> 00:20:24,500
Well, hey, what about him!

326
00:20:25,380 --> 00:20:26,020
Fire!

327
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:33,960
Just wait!

328
00:20:46,100 --> 00:20:47,260
The boss is getting away!

329
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:52,660
They won't come this far.

330
00:20:52,660 --> 00:20:55,060
Even Cosmo can't handle the sea and sky.

331
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:00,780
He's going to escape!

332
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:02,240
But...

333
00:21:02,780 --> 00:21:05,300
Now's our chance to win a
battle and earn some credit!

334
00:21:05,300 --> 00:21:06,440
Fly, Jin-1!

335
00:21:08,260 --> 00:21:09,120
It takes guts!

336
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:10,640
If you try, you can do it!

337
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,844
Ugh, ugh...

338
00:21:13,894 --> 00:21:16,900
Ugh, ugh, ugh...

339
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:20,260
Yo-chan! What are you planning to do?!

340
00:21:20,260 --> 00:21:22,700
Ugh, ugh, ugh, ugh...

341
00:21:22,700 --> 00:21:25,260
Fly! Guts!

342
00:21:25,460 --> 00:21:27,722
Ugh, ugh...

343
00:21:27,772 --> 00:21:29,700
Ugh, ugh...

344
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,940
Ryo-sama!

345
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:43,340
Senpai is

346
00:21:46,920 --> 00:21:49,040
No way, that Ryotsu guy

347
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:51,640
Ryo-chan, Lord Ryo

348
00:21:55,700 --> 00:21:56,500
Senpai!

349
00:21:56,580 --> 00:21:58,400
Lord Ryo! It's Ryo-san, right!

350
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:58,680
Ryotsu!

351
00:21:59,060 --> 00:22:01,080
I'll save you now, Z1!

352
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:09,032
Hang in there,

353
00:22:09,082 --> 00:22:10,540
Z1!

354
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:15,060
Yeah, right! This won't bring me down!

355
00:22:15,980 --> 00:22:17,240
Z1!

356
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:18,729
Ryotsuuu,

357
00:22:18,779 --> 00:22:22,800
We were the best partners, weren't we?

358
00:22:23,620 --> 00:22:25,900
Yeah, we were the best partners.

359
00:22:25,900 --> 00:22:28,600
So don't die, don't you dare die, Z1!

360
00:22:29,860 --> 00:22:31,520
Ryotsuuu

361
00:22:33,040 --> 00:22:36,320
Z1! Z1!

362
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:41,120
I'll never forget you! Z1!

363
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:51,280
Gentlemen,
the Chief is scheduled to inspect us today.

364
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:52,500
The Chief.

365
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:55,740
Ryotsu,
make sure there's no rudeness whatsoever.

366
00:22:56,520 --> 00:22:58,980
The Chief has arrived.

367
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:05,460
Listen up, I am the Chief,
and my ego is very high.

368
00:23:07,140 --> 00:23:10,820
Look, I've been revived, just like this.

369
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:14,120
But after that recent achievement,
I won't take the environment lightly.

370
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:15,440
What was that?

371
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:19,820
Rose, I think I'll have you
wax me again after so long.

372
00:23:19,820 --> 00:23:23,820
Ohara, you do the glass polishing,
and the Chief will handle the rest.

373
00:23:24,180 --> 00:23:29,180
Hey, Reiko, Maria-kun, how about a
drive together to Rainbow Bridge sometime?

374
00:23:29,540 --> 00:23:32,160
He came back even more selfish than before.

375
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:35,060
All the tears I shed, what were they for?

376
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:39,420
Why didn't you sink Tokyo Bay back then?

377
00:23:39,420 --> 00:23:41,000
Don't say something like that to me.

378
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:43,660
Hey! Ohara, Ryotsu!

379
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:44,700
Y-yes, sir!

380
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:48,160
What are you two doing? Hurry up and listen!

381
00:23:48,780 --> 00:23:50,780
We're back, Chief!

382
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:53,170
The right side is still dirty.

383
00:23:53,220 --> 00:23:55,300
President, knead harder, please.

384
00:23:55,420 --> 00:23:56,780
That spot feels great!

385
00:23:57,200 --> 00:24:00,180
I can't take this selfish boss anymore!

386
00:24:04,720 --> 00:24:11,880
Oden, ramen, beer! Get your hands on the mass-produced yatai everyone's talking about!
It's you again, Bakuryu's old man!

387
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:17,540
Please, don't get in the way of my business!
What's that? That's a bomb!

388
00:24:17,540 --> 00:24:21,260
Next time: Super-Speed Yatai Showdown,
see you!

389
00:24:35,760 --> 00:24:44,100
Surprise, and noise, and spirit, and
solution, and quickness, and helping out.

390
00:24:44,100 --> 00:24:55,700
Decided, and flash of inspiration, and bouncing,
and wrapping up, and action, and flying away.

391
00:24:56,640 --> 00:25:00,520
Above all, an amazing power.

392
00:25:00,520 --> 00:25:12,700
Everyone, gather! Come here,
and it's a dreamlike final energy.

393
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:23,820
Gaze at tomorrow, believe in yesterday, paint the universe, and stand on the ground.
Kameari's star spun around in a circle.

394
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:29,040
Is this good enough? Like hell it is!

395
00:25:37,600 --> 00:25:43,520
Thank you for watching.

